<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      LAUNCH THEME ONLY. Everything after the first frame is Compose, themed by
      DistrictTheme, which does its own light/dark selection. This style governs the
      window before Compose draws, so getting it wrong shows up as a flash of the
      wrong colour rather than a broken UI.

      Parent is a PLATFORM theme, not a Material Components one, so the app does not
      need appcompat or the Material views library on its classpath purely to satisfy
      an XML parent. NoActionBar because ComponentActivity provides no action bar and
      inheriting one draws a stripe above the Compose content.

      ⚠️ VERIFIED AGAINST android.jar, NOT ASSUMED. `Theme.DeviceDefault.DayNight`
      exists but has NO `.NoActionBar` variant — the obvious-looking
      `Theme.DeviceDefault.DayNight.NoActionBar` does not exist and fails resource
      linking with "resource android:style/... not found". The DayNight parent is
      also API 29+, so this baseline stays on the Light variant and values-v29/
      overrides it. Confirmed by extracting android/R$style from the platform jar.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.DistrictAI" parent="@android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">?android:attr/colorBackground</item>
    </style>
</resources>
